                    <div class="testimonial-content-box bg_cover wow fadeInRight justify-content-center   d-flex flex-column" style="background-image: none !important; visibility: visible; animation-name: fadeInRight;">
                        <p><strong>What factors should you consider when purchasing a cat or kitten?</strong></p>
                        <p>Discover how we can assist you in making this challenging decision.</p>

                        <p>&nbsp;</p>
                        <p>Kittens are undeniably adorable, (and they are well aware of it), but their cuteness should not be the only factor in choosing a cat. When making the decision to bring a cat or kitten into your home, it is a significant, yet thrilling commitment that requires careful consideration. It is essential to conduct thorough research and select a reputable breeder who prioritizes the well-being of their cats and kittens. Visiting the breeder in person allows you to observe first hand how the cats are raised and cared for.</p>
                        <p>Cats make wonderful companions and enrich our lives, but it is crucial to ensure that you have the time and resources to provide them with proper care both now and in the future. Owning a cat is a long-term commitment that can span over a decade or more. Particularly with kittens, their care and attention needs will evolve as they grow, so it is vital to contemplate whether this aligns with your lifestyle in the coming months.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

            </div>

        </div>
    </div>

</section>

<section class="testimonial-area     pb-0 pt-0" style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(77, 79, 95, 1), rgba(77, 79, 95, 1)) !important;">
    <div class="container py-5">
        <div class="testimonial-wrapper-two">
            <div class="row no-gutters" style=" visibility: visible; animation-name: fadeInRight; row-gap: 30px;">

                <div class="col-lg-6 d-flex order-1-class justify-content-center align-items-center pr-lg-3">
                    <div class="testimonial-content-box bg_cover wow fadeInRight justify-content-center   d-flex flex-column" style="background-image: none !important; visibility: visible; animation-name: fadeInRight;">

                        <p><span style="color: #ffffff;">A kitten should not be separated from its mother until it is at least twelve weeks old, and if a kitten is crossing borders, it should be fifteen weeks old before leaving. Therefore, it is important to stay informed about their age and verify this information. When interacting with a responsible breeder, they will have knowledge of the kitten's birthplace, parents, and behaviour, and will be happy to provide you with these details.</span></p>


                        <p><span style="color: #ffffff;">Before deciding to bring the kitten home, it's important to inquire about any nervousness or health issues the kitten may have. During your visit to pick up your new pet, be attentive to any concerns raised and watch for signs of potential problems. It's recommended that kittens receive worming, flea treatment, and their initial vaccination at 9 weeks of age, followed by a second vaccination at 12 to 15 weeks. Make sure to ask about these treatments and request a copy of the records beforehand. All vaccination details are documented in an animal passport by a qualified veterinarian.</span></p>


                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-6 order-2-class d-flex ">
